The previous crop was wheat, which belongs to the cereal family. Faba bean and lentil are therefore favored as legume alternatives that avoid repeating the previous crop family across the complete farm. Barley, wheat, and forage oats remain in the allocation because the model balances rotation with environmental suitability, food production, and livestock-feed needs.

